.TH RRDRECONCILE 8 "Version 4.3.30:  4 Sep 2019" "Xymon"
.SH NAME
rrdreconcile \- bring existing RRD files in line with the declared schema
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "rrdreconcile [options]"

.SH DESCRIPTION
An RRD file keeps the schema it was created with. Two declarations
that shape a file can change afterwards, and then only new files
follow them:

.IP \(bu 3
the consolidation functions (AVERAGE, MIN, MAX, LAST) that the
matching
.I graphs.cfg(5)
definitions read in their DEF lines, which
.I xymond_rrd(8)
uses to choose a new file's archives;
.IP \(bu 3
the dataset heartbeats a status message declares in its XYMON METRICS
block, which
.I xymond_rrd(8)
records in each host's fileset index.
.PP
rrdreconcile walks the RRD directory and compares the files of each
host against these declarations: the files its fileset index lists, or,
for a host without an index, every .rrd file in its directory (archives
only then, since the heartbeats come from the index). It repairs the
divergence
with "rrdtool tune": a changed heartbeat is set on the dataset, and a
missing consolidation function gets one archive for each existing
AVERAGE archive, with the same geometry.

By default it only prints the plan. With \-\-apply it runs it. It
never changes a file on its own initiative, and xymond_rrd never runs
it: run it by hand, or from cron, after changing graphs.cfg DEF lines
or the heartbeats a producer declares.

The repairs work forward only. An added archive starts empty and fills
from now on; the history already consolidated into other archives is
not copied into it. A changed heartbeat applies to future updates;
gaps already recorded as unknown stay unknown.

For a file with more than 64 archives, adding archives is skipped and
reported; its heartbeats are still reconciled. An index entry whose
name would leave the host's directory is skipped.

.SH OPTIONS
.IP "\-\-apply"
Run the repairs instead of only printing them.
.IP "\-\-dry\-run"
Only print the repairs. This is the default.
.IP "\-\-rrddir=DIRECTORY"
The RRD directory to walk. Defaults to $XYMONRRDS.
.IP "\-\-host=HOSTNAME"
Only reconcile this host's files.
.IP "\-\-config=FILENAME"
The graphs.cfg file to read the definitions from. Defaults to
$XYMONHOME/etc/graphs.cfg.
.IP "\-\-rrdtool=PATH"
The rrdtool command to run. Defaults to "rrdtool", found in the PATH.
Adding archives needs rrdtool 1.5 or later.
.IP "\-\-env=FILENAME"
Load the environment from FILENAME, for example xymonserver.cfg, to
find $XYMONRRDS and $XYMONHOME.
.IP "\-\-area=NAME"
The environment area to use with \-\-env.
.IP "\-\-debug"
Print debugging output.

.SH "EXIT STATUS"
0 when every file conforms or every repair succeeded, 1 when a repair
failed or the RRD directory cannot be read.

.SH "SEE ALSO"
xymond_rrd(8), graphs.cfg(5), xymonserver.cfg(5), rrdtool(1)
